---
description: Git branch naming and worktree isolation rules for issue fixing
---
# Git Branch and Worktree Rules

## Branch Naming Convention
- Feature branches for issue fixes: `batch-fix-{ISSUES}` where {ISSUES} is hyphen-separated (e.g., `batch-fix-105-106-107`)
- Source branch: `upstream/main` (tracks GitHub main branch)
- Target branch: `main` (PRs merge here)
- Worktree paths: `../issue{ISSUENUM}-worktree` for per-issue worktrees
- Batch worktree: `../batch-fix-worktree`

## Branch Hygiene Rules
1. `upstream/main` = GitHub main branch (read from remote, push back after PR merge)
2. Local `upstream/main` tracks GitHub main (git fetch upstream)
3. Feature branch created from local `upstream/main` state
4. AFTER PR MERGE: sync GitHub `upstream` to match merged `main`
5. Never push local upstream to GitHub main (would overwrite merged changes)
6. After merge: push merged commit to GitHub upstream branch

## Worktree Isolation Rules
1. Per-issue worktrees for isolation (one per issue)
2. Batch worktree for accumulating changes
3. Sequential issue processing, parallel cluster processing
4. Remove issue worktrees after cherry-pick to batch
5. Keep batch worktree for debugging if batch fails

## Commit Message Rules
- Subagent commits: `[AUTO] Issue $ISSUE - Cluster {id}: {summary}`
- Batch commit: `feat: resolve issues $ISSUES - batch fix` with issue list and validation summary
